                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119904">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119904</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153284</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119904</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1252920307">DTC_L3_MU_BIST</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_272524571">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MU_BIST" is  set:
1a.) if the LBIST_OK bit of the BIST register reports a "Logic Bild in Self Test failure"
    [(BIST: LBIST_OK == 0) 
1b.) or the ABIST1_OK bit of the BIST register reports a "Analog Build in Self Test 1 failure" and the Fail Safe Output has no short circuit to high"
||  (BIST: ABIST1_OK == 0) 
1c.) or the ABIST2_VAUX_OK bit of the BIST register reports a "Analog Build in Self Test 2 - VAUX failure or not executed" if VAUX will be used safety critical
||   ((BIST: ABIST2_VAUX_OK == 0) &amp;&amp; ((VAUX_FS_OV_1:0 != 00) || (VAUX_FS_UV_1:0 != 00))
1d.) or if a device with FS1B output is present and the ABIST2_FS1B_OK bit of the BIST register reports a "Analog Build in Self Test 2 - FS1b failure or not executed"
(BIST: ABIST2_FS1B == 0) &amp;&amp; (DEVICE_ID_FS.FS1 == 1)]</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1199F1">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1199F1</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153521</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P1199F1</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_370139176">DTC_L3_MU_ERR_INT</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1690865650">Cyclic 1ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1754934901">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MU_ERR_INT" is set:
1a.) if the Monitoring Unit reports an error from an internal redundant structure of the Fail-safe state machine and the information is received "valid" via SPI  
(ERR_INT_HW == 1) &amp;&amp; (SPI_G == 0)
1b.) or if the Monitoring Unit reports an error from the EDC (Error Detection Correction) of the Fail-safe state machine and the information is received "valid" via SPI
|| (ERR_INT_SW == 1) &amp;&amp; (SPI_G == 0)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119983">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119983</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153411</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119983</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_796482306">DTC_L3_MU_SPI_COM</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1690865650">Cyclic 1ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_80373928"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_MU_SPI_COM" shall be set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1)
3.) and the WD_BAD_TIMING bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "wrong WD timing refresh" or the WD_BAD_DATA bit reports a "wrong WD data refresh"
&& ((WD_ANSWER: WD_BAD_TIMING == 1) || (WD_ANSWER: WD_BAD_DATA == 1))
4.) and the marker in the reset proof RAM indicates a erroneous SPI communication
&& (RPRAM_DiagSPI == 1)]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1199A1">
