                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_2054601980">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MU_LSU_CONFIG" is set:
1a.) if the VCCA_PNP_DETECT bit of the HW_CONFIG register reports that a "External PNP is connected" although "Internal Mosfet detection" is expected
(HW_CONFIG: VCCA_PNP_DET == 0)    
1b.) or the VCCA_HW bit of the HW_CONFIG register reports a "3.3 V configuration" although a "5.0V configuration" is expected
||   (HW_CONFIG: VCCA_HW == 0)
1c.) or the VAUX_HW bit of the HW_CONFIG register reports a "3.3 V configuration" although a "5.0 V configuration" is expected
(HW_CONFIG: VAUX_HW == 1)
1d1.) or in case of (SBC_VPRE_CONFIG == 0) if the LS_DETECT bit of the HW_CONFIG register reports that a "Buck-Boost" is detected although "Buck only" is expected
(HW_CONFIG.LS_DETECT == 0)  
1d2.) or in case of (SBC_VPRE_CONFIG == 1) if the LS_DETECT bit of the HW_CONFIG register reports that a "Buck only" is detected although "Buck-Boost" is expected
(HW_CONFIG.LS_DETECT == 1)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119956">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119956</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153366</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119956</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1250253740">DTC_L3_MU_HW_CONFIG</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_286773328">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MU_HW_CONFIG" is set:
#### PATH 1 ####
1a.) if the DBG_HW bit of the HW_CONFIG register reports "Debug mode selected" although "Normal operation" is expected
(HW_CONFIG: DBG_HW == 1)
#### PATH 2 ####
1b1.) if the DFS_HW1 bit of the HW_CONFIG register reports "Deep Fail Safe function is disabled" although "Deep Fail Safe function enabled" is expected
(HW_CONFIG: DFS_HW1 == 0) 
1b2.) or if the DFS_HW2 bit of the DEVICE_ID_FS register reports "Deep Fail Safe function is disabled" although "Deep Fail Safe function enabled" is expected 
||   (DEVICE_ID_FS: DFS_HW2 == 0)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119955">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119955</SHORT-NAME>
