2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1787509172">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MU_SMU_CON_CHECK" is set:
#### Path 1 - SMU Pull Down Resistor Check ####
1a.) if the readback value "state_P33.8" is not "low" as expected during the SMU_FSP (P33.8) is configured as input with pull up device
(state_P33.8 != 0b)
#### Path 2 - SMU Connection Check ####
2a.) if the readback value "state_IO2L" is not "low" as expected (Activated FSP) during the SMU_FSP output of the MCU is set to "low"
(state_IO2L != 0) 
2b.) or if the readback value "state_IO2H" is not "high" as expected (Release FSP) during the SMU_FSP output of the MCU is set to "high"
|| (state_IO2H != 1)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
