                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119A04">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119A04</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153540</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119A04</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_299667151">DTC_L3_MCU_LBIST</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1566387392">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_LBIST" is set if:
##### Path 1 - direct after execution during Cold Porst #####
1a.) the MISR signature read from the LBIST3 Control Registers is not equal the expected value
(LBISTCTRL3.SIGNATURE != 0x4072038C) 
1b.) or the "LBIST Execution Indicator" doesn't indicate "that the LBIST procedure has been successfully finished since last power on reset" within a specified time span
||   (SCU_LBISTCTRL0.LBISTDONE != 1)
1c.) or the LBPORST bit in the Reset Status Register indicates that the LBIST execution was terminated earlier due to a PORST assertion
||   (SCU_RSTSTAT.LBPORST == 1) 
1d.) or the LBTERM bit in the Reset Status Register indicates that the LBIST execution was not terminated properly
||   (SCU_RSTSTAT.LBTERM == 0) 

##### Path 2 - after SBC Init Timeout #####
if the MCU is starting up after a "SBC reset caused by a Init Timeout" and the "LBIST after the Cold porst before was not successfull" 
2a.) (RPRAM_LBIST_Result != 0xA5A5A5A5) &amp;&amp; (RPRAM_SBC_InitTimeout == 1) </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119A01">
