                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_958195152">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_FW_CHECK" is set if:
1a.) the "SMU_core Alarm Status flags" are "not as expected"
(SMU_AG0 != 0x2490) || (SMU_AG1 != 0x2490) || (SMU_AG2 != 0x2490) || (SMU_AG3 != 0x2490) || (SMU_AG4 != 0x0) || (SMU_AG5 != 0x0) || 
(SMU_AG6 != 0x124800) || (SMU_AG7 != 0x2) || (SMU_AG8 != 0x20) || (SMU_AG9 == 0x0) || (SMU_AG10 != 0x0) || (SMU_AG11 != 0x0)   
1b.) or the "Start-up Memory Registers" are "not as expected"
||   (SCU_STMEM3 != A030 FB1F) || (SCU_STMEM4 != 00000001) || (SCU_STMEM5 != A030 FB1F) || (SCU_STMEM6 != A030 FB1F)
1c.) or the "Lockstep Control Registers" are "not as expected"
||   (SCU_LCLCON0 != 0x8001 0000) || (SCU_LCLCON1 == 0x8001 0000) 
1d.) or the "Memory ECC Detection Registers" are "not as expected"
||   (MCi_ECCD != 0x5) (i=0-95)
1e.) or the "SSH Safety Faults Status Registers" are "not as expected"
||   (MCi_FAULTSTS != 0x9) (initialized RAM) (i= 0-95)                           // initialzed RAM
1f.) or the "Error Information Registers" are "not as expected"
||   (MCi_ERRINFOx != 0x0) (i=0-95, x=0-4) </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
