                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119A4B</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_357908207">DTC_L3_MCU_SMU_DTS_TEMP_HIGH</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_2006643246"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_SMU_DTS_TEMP_HIGH" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

#### Path 1 - Core Domain Die Temperature Sensor - SMUCore ####
4a.) and the Core Domain Die Temperature Sensor reports a "Over Temperature Alarm" in the SMU Alarm Status Register
&& [(SMU_AG8.SF31) 

#### Path 2 - PMS Die Temperature Sensor - SMUCore ####
4b.) or the PMS Die Temperature Sensor reports a "Temperature Overflow Alarm" in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG9.SF0) 

#### Path 3 - PMS Die Temperature Sensor - SMUStandby ####
4c.) or the PMS Die Temperature Sensor reports a "Temperature Overflow Alarm" in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG21.SF9)]]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119AFE">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119AFE</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153790</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119AFE</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
