                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1186912015"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_SMU_CLOCK" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

#### Path 1 - Clock Monitor ####
4a.) and a "OSC clock frequency out of range" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
&& [(SMU_AG8.SF0) 
4b.) or a "Back-up clock out-of-range alarm" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG8.SF1) 

#### Path 2 - Clock Alive Monitor ####
4c.) or a "Back-up clock alive alarm" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG8.SF2) 
4d.) or a "Clock Alive alarm" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG21.SF15)

#### Path 3 - PLL loss of lock detection ####
4e.) or a "System PLL DCO loss of lock event" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG8.SF3) 
4f.) or a "Peripheral PLL DCO loss of lock event" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG8.SF4) 

#### Path 4 - Clock plausibilization ####
4g.) or a "Clock Plausibilization event" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG10.SF12)

#### Path 5 - System Timer Monitoring ####
4h.) or a "STM0 to SMT1 mismatch event" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG10.SF13)]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
