                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1725536018"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_SMU_PFLASH" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

#### Path 1 - PFlash Read Path Error Monitor ####
4a.) and a "CPU0 PFLASH0 Read Path Error" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
&& [(SMU_AG0.SF2) 
4b.) or a "CPU1 PFLASH1 Read Path Error" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG1.SF2) 

#### Path 2 - PFlash Singlebit / Doublebit / Multibit Correction Tracking Buffer ####
4c.) or a "Single Bit Correction Tracking Buffer Full" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF24) 
4d.) or a "Double Bit Correction Tracking Buffer Full" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF25) 
4e.) or a "Multiple Bit Correction Tracking Buffer Full" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF26) 
4f.) or a "Zero Bit Correction Tracking Buffer Full" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF27) 

#### Path 3 - PFlash ECC / EDC Error ####
4g.) or a "PFlash ECC" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF28) 
4h.) or a "PFlash EDC" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF29) 

#### Path 4 - PFlash Configuration Error ####
4i.) or a "CPU FLASHCON Configuration Error" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF30) 
4j.) or a "Flash Stored Configuration Error" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
|| (SMU_AG7.SF31)]]]></SD>
