                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_177251977">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_SMU_BUS" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&amp;&amp; (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&amp;&amp; ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

#### Path 1 - SRI / End to End EDC CPU 0/1 #### 
4a.) a "CPU0 Instruction Fetch SRI Interface EDC Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register    	(RP_RAM_SMU_AG0.SF22) 
4b.) a "CPU1 Instruction Fetch SRI Interface EDC Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG1.SF22) 
4c.) a "CPU0 Data SRI Interface (Load/Store) EDC Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG0.SF23) 
4d.) a "CPU1 Data SRI Interface (Load/Store) EDC Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG1.SF23) 
4e.) a "XBAR0 Bus Error Event / EndInit / SafteyEndInit Register Protection Event" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG7.SF17)

#### Path 2 - SPB Error Detection ####
4f.) a "SPB Bus Error Event / / EndInit / SafteyEndInit Register Protection Event" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG7.SF20)

#### Path 3 - DMA SRI ECC ####
4g.) a "DMA SRI ECC Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG8.SF23)

#### Path 4 - SRI Error Detetcion Code EDC #### 
4h.) a "Xbar EDC Address Phase Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG11.SF2) 
4i.) a "Xbar EDC Write Phase Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG11.SF3) 
4j.) a "DMU Address Phase Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG11.SF4) 
4k.) a "DMU EDC Write Phase Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG11.SF5) 
4l.) a "SPB EDC Read Phase Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG11.SF9) 

#### Path 5 - Converter Phase Synchronizer #### 
4m.) a "Converter Phase Synchronizer Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG11.SF12) 
  
#### Path 6 - SRI SOTA Monitor ###2
4n.) a "SOTA Swap Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RP_RAM_SMU_AG11.SF13)
</SD>
