                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119AF8">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119AF8</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153784</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119AF8</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1916783429">DTC_L3_MCU_SMU_EXCEPTION_CORE</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1370316828"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_SMU_EXCEPTION_CORE" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

#### Path 1 - Exception Monitor CPU 0/1 ####
4a.) and a "CPU0/1 exception (interrupt/trap)" is reported in the SMU Alarm Status Register
&& [(SMU_AG0.SF24) || (SMU_AG1.SF24)]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119AF9">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119AF9</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153785</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119AF9</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1295162771">DTC_L3_MCU_SMU_SAFETY_FLIP_FLOP</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1873284423">The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_SMU_SAFETY_FLIP_FLOP" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&amp;&amp; (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&amp;&amp; ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

### Path 1 - PMS Safety flip-flops ####
4a.) a "PMS Safety flip-flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register   
(RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF5 == 1)
4b.) or a "Miscellaneous safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG10.SF21 == 1) 

#### Path 2 - Clock Safety flip-flops ####
4c.) or a "SYS_PLL / PER_PLL safety flip flop alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF8 == 1) 
4d.) or a "CCU safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF24 == 1) 
4e.) or a "CCU safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF25 == 1) 
4f.) or a "CCU safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG10.SF20 == 1) 

#### Path 3 - Further Safety flip-flops ####
4g.) or a "MTU safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF0 == 1) 
4h.) or a "GTM / IOM safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF1 == 1) 
4i.) or a "INT safety flip flop uncorrectable alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF2 == 1) 
4j.) or a "SCU safety flip flop uncorrectable alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF4 == 1) 
4k.) or a "DMA safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is stored is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF6 == 1) 
4l.) or a "SMU_CORE safety flip flop uncorrectable error alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF7 == 1) 
4m.) or a "Cerberus / Debug safety flip flop uncorrectable alarm is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SF23 == 1) 
4n.) or a "Safety safety flip flop uncorrectable alarm is indicated in the SMU_Stby"
||   (SMU_AG21.SF7 == 1) 

#### Path 4 - Interrupt Configuration Monitor ####
4o.) a "EDC Configuration and Data Path Error" is indicated in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core Alarm Status Register
||   (RPRAM_SMU_AG8.SF22)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
