                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119BFB</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1154043</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119BFB</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_21979711">DTC_L1_NVM_INFO</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_990400465">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent1.a) replace the ECU(Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECUspecial measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1196308264">The failure will be set:
1. Layout Version mismatch detected 
2. No complete sector, sector switch count indicates initialisation phase =&gt; interrupted NVM initialisation - reinitialize *
3. Find next Block Header is not possible (Read failed)
4. Block head read out invalid class Id
5. Block data read is not possible (Read failed)
6. Block data CRC failure
7. Header pattern is not as expected</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119B41">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119B41</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153857</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119B41</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1853232192">DTC_L3_FLASH_CONSISTENCY</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1086091511">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) update or reflash the ECU
1.b) replace the ECU(Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECUspecial measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1190974734"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_FLASH_CONSISTENCY" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

4a.) and the Monitoring Function has triggered the "SW Alarm 7" which is reported in the SMU_core Alarm Status Register
&& (SMU_AG10.SF7 ==1)
4b.) The calculated CRC value of a block  is unequal to the expected value. The check is done for application and dataset.
* number of checked elements is not equal to table entries
* calculated CRC32 for sector is not equal to stored one]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119BFC">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119BFC</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1154044</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119BFC</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1504974951">DTC_L1_INCOMPLETE_SHDWN</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_267704555">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent1.a) check wiring harness and connector(s)1.b) check other ECU for low voltage events(Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECUspecial measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_960037676">The failure will be set:
If consecutive times a voltage loss on KL30/KL30 happends (line break), in that case the shutdown procedure is not successful finished. The count of consecutive voltage loss is a parameter.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1194F0">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1194F0</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1152240</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P1194F0</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_37602652">DTC_L3_SUPERVISON_L2_EMERGENCY_STOP</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1606288301"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_SUPERVISION_L2_EMERGENCY" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

4.) and a "Recovery Timer 1 -  Time-out Alarm" is reported in the SMU_core Alarm Status Register
&& (SMU_AG10.SF17 ==1)
5.) and a "External Emergency Stop Signal Event Alarm" is reported in the SMU_core Alarm Status Register
&& (SMU_AG8.SF19 == 1)
]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1194F1">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1194F1</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1152241</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P1194F1</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1539945923">DTC_L3_SUPERVISON_L2_IO_MONITORING</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1307129560">At Execution time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1751590900"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_SUPERVISION_L2_IO_MONITORING" is set:
1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 

3a.) and either the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
3b.) or the reset proof RAM marker indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed SMU reaction (e.g. SMU_FSP stuck at high)
|| (RPRAM_IntendedWD_Error))

4.) and a "Recovery Timer 1 -  Time-out Alarm" is reported in the SMU_core Alarm Status Register
&& (SMU_AG10.SF17 ==1)
5.) and a "IO Monitoring Pin Mismatch Indication Alarm" is reported in the SMU_core Alarm Status Register
&& (SMU_AG8.SF25 == 1)]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP119AF0">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP119AF0</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1153776</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P119AF0</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_867000429">DTC_L3_MCU_UNEXPECTED_RESET</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_394013032"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_MCU_UNEXPECTED_RESET" is set if:

#### Path 1 - Reset due to IO2 - without information in the SMU Alarm Registers #####
1a.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2a.) and the RSTb_EXT bit of the DIAG_SF_IOs  register doesn't report a " external Reset"
(DIAG_SF_IOs: RSTB_EXT == 0)
3a.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 
4a.) and the IO23_FAIL bit of the DIAG_FS_IOs register reports an "IO23 monitoring error"
&& (DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) 
5a.) and no Alarm is present in SMU_Stdby 
&& ((SMU_AG20.SFx == 0) && (SMU_AG21.SFx == 0))
6a.) and no Alarm is present in the reset proof RAM copy of the SMU_Core
&& ((RPRAM_SMU_AG0.SFx == 0) && (RPRAM_SMU_AG1.SFx == 0) && (RPRAM_SMU_AG6.SFx == 0) && (RPRAM_SMU_AG7.SFx == 0) && (RPRAM_SMU_AG8.SFx == 0) && (RPRAM_SMU_AG9.SFx == 0) && (RPRAM_SMU_AG10.SFx == 0))



#### Path 2 - Reset due to IO2 or WD Refresh a cascading reset of an unexpected system or application reset #####
1b.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)    
2b.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1) 
3b.) and the IO23_FAIL bit reports an "IO23 monitoring error" or the WD_BAD_TIMING bit reports a "WD refresh in the wrong WD window"
&& ((DIAG_SF_IOs: IO_23_FAIL == 1) || (WD_ANSWER: WD_BAD_TIMING == 1))
4b.) and the reset proof RAM flag which indicates a system or application reset is set
&& (RPRAM_UnexpectedResetFlag == true) ***

Note***:  the flag RPRAM_UnexpectedResetFlag is set if  "Start-up Memory Registers" indicates that the MCU ist starting up from a "System Reset" or "Application Reset" (SCU_STMEM3.APPR_CS == 1) || (SCU_STMEM3.SYSR_CS == 1)]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP2D9EA2">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP2D9EA2</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>2989730</TROUBLE-CODE>
