                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP1196F3">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP1196F3</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>1152755</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>P1196F3</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_464803850">DTC_L3_MU_nSSP3_CHECK</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>0</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_487698118">Case 1.) if error occurrence counter &gt;=3 or if the failure is permanent
1.a) replace the ECU (Control units commissioning as specified in technical product description)

Case2.) otherwise (error occurrence counter &lt;= 2 and failure is not permanent)
2.a.) Delete error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.b.) Perform test of the system functionality (&lt;customer specific&gt;)
2.c.) read again error memory entry (&lt;customer specific&gt;), if error memory entry is still present - replace the ECU

special measure: SW update (potential errata) in case of SW dependant known issues</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_474518921">EDM_SYSTEMCOND_ALWAYS_ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_713037638">Startup/Initialization</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1724367786"><![CDATA[The failure event "EVENT_L3_MU_nSSP3_CHECK" is set:

####  PATH1 - SSP2 Pull Up Resistor Check ####
1a.) the readback value of the SSP2 MCU output is not "high" as expected while the MCU open collector output port is not driven to "low"
(SSP2_Fb == 0b)
  
####  PATH2 - nSSP3 Initial State Check ####
1b1.) or the readback value of the safe state path 3 via MCU port input is not "asserted" as expected although the safe state output is not yet released (neither MCU SSP2 nor SBC FS0b)
|| (nSSP3_Fb == released)
1b2.) or the readback value of the safe state path 3 via SPI from the SBC is not "low" as expected although the safe state output is not yet released (neither MCU SSP2 nor SBC FS0b)
|| (nSSP3_FS0b_SNS == 1)

####  PATH3 - nSSP3 Low State Check - Asserted by FS65xx ####
1c.) or the readback value of the safe state path 3 via MCU port input is not "asserted" as expected although the safe state output is not yet released (still asserted by SBC FS0b while MCU SSP2 is already released)
|| (nSSP3_Fb == released)

####  PATH4 - nSSP3 High State Check - Released by FS65xx ####
1d1.) or the readback value of the safe state path 3 via MCU port input is not "released" as expected although the safe state output is  released (by MCU SSP2 and SBC FS0b)
|| (nSSP3_Fb == asserted)
1d2.) or the readback value of the safe state path 3 via SPI from the SBC is not "high" as expected although the safe state output is  released (by MCU SSP2 and SBC FS0b)
|| (nSSP3_FS0b_SNS == 0)

####  PATH5 - nSSP3 Low State Check - Asserted by MCU ####
1e.) or the readback value of the safe state path 3 via MCU port input is not "asserted" as expected although the safe state output is not yet released (still asserted by MCU SSP2 while SBC FS0b is already released)
|| (nSSP3_Fb == released)

####  PATH6 - SAFE_STATE_REQUESTED not executed ####

1.) if the RSTb bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Reset"
(WD_ANSWER: RSTB == 1)
2.) and the FSxB bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "Fail-safe event"
&& (WD_ANSWER: FSxB == 1)
3.) and the WD_BAD_DATA bit of the WD ANSWER register reports a "wrong WD data refresh"
&& (WD_ANSWER: WD_BAD_DATA == 1)
4.) and the marker in the reset proof RAM indicates that the wrong WD data refresh was provoked due to a not executed "Safe State Assert" 
&& (RPRAM_nSSP3_AssertError == 1)
]]></SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1999390981">0</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_MCU_F.BV.BV_MCU_F.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCP065717">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCP065717</SHORT-NAME>
